[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FreyByyy/TimeToGraze/main/About/Preview.png[/img]

[h1]Your herd deserves fresh grass.[/h1]

Penned animals eat their pen bare, and the rest of the map is a sea of free grass they never get to touch. [b]Time to Graze[/b] fixes that. When the herd gets hungry, your handlers rope everyone up, lead them out to a pasture, let them graze, and bring them home again. All of it happens on its own.

Want to keep the herd safe out there? Assign a [b]shepherd[/b] and a [b]herding dog[/b]. Fewer animals wander off, predators think twice, and the shepherd enjoys a quiet day under the open sky.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FreyByyy/TimeToGraze/main/Workshop/images/b_fieldguide/header_en.png[/img]

[h2]Pasture zone[/h2]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FreyByyy/TimeToGraze/main/Workshop/images/b_fieldguide/pasture_en.png[/img]
A new [b]Pasture[/b] zone in the Zones menu. Draw it on any open grassland, then link it to a pen. You can link several pastures to one pen: the herd always goes to the one with the most grass, so the others have time to regrow.
[list]
[*] Animals stay inside the pasture while they graze and keep eating until they are full.
[*] Hide or show pastures like any other zone.
[/list]

[h2]Grazing tab on the pen marker[/h2]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FreyByyy/TimeToGraze/main/Workshop/images/b_fieldguide/tab_en.png[/img]
Everything is set per pen:
[list]
[*][b]When to go out:[/b] an animal's fullness drops below X%, the pen is running out of food, or fixed grazing hours.
[*][b]When to come back:[/b] everyone is fed, the grazing hours end or night falls, or danger appears.
[*][b]Herd filter:[/b] keep the sick, the pregnant or the young at home, or exclude any single animal.
[*][b]Go graze / Bring herd back[/b] buttons for manual control.
[/list]

[h2]Leading the herd[/h2]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FreyByyy/TimeToGraze/main/Workshop/images/b_fieldguide/lead_en.png[/img]
Any colonist with the Handling work type ropes up the [b]whole herd at once[/b] and leads it out, then brings it back the same way. It uses the vanilla roping mechanics, with no teleporting and no magic.

[h2]Shepherd & herding dog[/h2]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FreyByyy/TimeToGraze/main/Workshop/images/b_fieldguide/guards_en.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Shepherd:[/b] a chosen colonist who leads the herd out first and then stands watch for the whole grazing. Higher Animals skill means a stronger effect. Earns Animals XP and a small "quiet day at the pasture" mood bonus.
[*][b]Herding dog:[/b] a new [b]Herding[/b] training for huskies, labradors, Yorkshire terriers, wolves and wargs. The dog stays with the herd and goes for predators that hunt it.
[*]Grazing animals can still wander off, but much less often. With a shepherd and a dog it almost never happens.
[*]Predators are less likely to pick a guarded animal, and guards can chase them away.
[/list]

[h2]Danger[/h2]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FreyByyy/TimeToGraze/main/Workshop/images/b_fieldguide/danger_en.png[/img]
A predator hunting the herd, toxic fallout or haze, and unsafe temperatures bring the herd home automatically. If [b]enemies[/b] show up, the game asks you whether to bring the herd back or let it keep grazing. Nothing is forbidden outright.

[h2]Settings[/h2]
Every chance can be tuned in the mod settings: wander-off and predator multipliers for unguarded, dog, shepherd and both, skill scaling, minimum and maximum time at pasture, and messages.

[hr][/hr]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FreyByyy/TimeToGraze/main/Workshop/images/b_fieldguide/compat_en.png[/img]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]RimWorld [b]1.6[/b] and [b]1.7[/b] (Waylith engine).
[*]Requires [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2009463077]Harmony[/url].
[*]No DLC required.
[*]Safe to add to an existing save. Pasture data is not written into the map's areas, so removing the mod mid-game will not break your save.
[*]Works with modded pen markers. Modded dog races can opt in to Herding by adding [i]TTG_Herding[/i] to [i]race/trainableTags[/i].
[*]Not tested with Multiplayer yet.
[/list]

[h2]Languages[/h2]
English, Russian.

[h2]Source[/h2]
[url=https://github.com/FreyByyy/TimeToGraze]GitHub[/url]. Bug reports and suggestions are welcome in the comments.
